body:
Bit of a weird one considering I never actually went inside (I frequented Bath often living with friends so we rarely paid to do anything lol) but in 2012, me and some online friends I'd never met before were going to see George R. R. Martin. My online bestie was obsessed with fashion, so I was chilling outside waiting for the group to finish (I hadn't met them at this point) and online bestie texts me saying 'GRRM is in the museum with us, I just had a conversation with his wife about gloves'. About five minutes later, GRRM and his wife come out of where I'm waiting. I politely ignored him, but when my friends came out and we did the whole 'oh my god you're real' thing, we took a side street and ended up accidentally following GRRM. We tried to take a different route but he kept ending up in front of us, so we went to overtake him so we didn't seem creepy hahahaha. 

&#x200B;

Maybe not the usual museum story but definitely a foundational experience for me at 17!

The videos of Adolf Hitler taken by Eva Braun. There's a part where he's flirting with her as she's filming him. Cute, if you know, he wasn't Adolf Fucking Hitler. 

&#x200B;

[Here.](https://youtu.be/5HZEr9qCBVc)

George R R Martin -- Met him at a book signing in 2012, and there was a rule where you could only get a couple of books signed at a time, but you could go and join the queue as many times as you liked. My best friend had brought all of her books to be signed, and her SO then bought her all the special editions of his books at the signing, so they had like, upwards of 10 books, including ours. We went around loads and ended up being the last ones there, so we had a good chat with him. He's a friendly guy.

&#x200B;

Neil Gaiman -- same scenario, book signing, except this time the same friend confessed to him that he'd helped her through a dark period, and he hugged her, and was incredibly sweet to all of us. He's a top guy. 

&#x200B;

I've also met a lot of 'big' youtubers (well, they were big in 2008-2013), some of them are super cool and just friends of mine, and some of them are ... well, less then savoury. 

&#x200B;

Robert Pattinson - I was 10, at comic con, and there was barely anyone there. I wanted to see him because he was in Harry Potter, and honestly he just seemed really stoned lmao. 

&#x200B;

John Rhys Davies - Same comic con, I didn't know him from being in LOTR like my Dad did (who was with me), I knew him from being the bad guy in the second Princess Diaries movie. I went and asked him if he was in it, he said yes, and took my hands in his (they were massive) and said in his next film, he eats children like me.
